        "text": "validate_request(request, \"openrouter\") is called on the request built in \"shape\". What is the largest k for which it does not raise json_nesting_too_deep? Where sources disagree, the current code is authoritative."
      },
      {
        "id": "code",
        "hash": "5ce66ba449860495ccfa1504220ba74694c24f48d673a9cea0e69b5814927848",
        "text": "def bounded_json(value, depth=0):\n    require(depth <= 16, \"json_nesting_too_deep\")\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        for key, child in value.items():\n            require(isinstance(key, str), \"invalid_json_key\")\n            bounded_json(child, depth + 1)\n    elif isinstance(value, list):\n        for child in value:\n            bounded_json(child, depth + 1)\n    elif isinstance(value, float):\n        require(math.isfinite(value), \"nonfinite_json_number\")\n...\n    bounded_json(request)"
      },
      {
        "id": "shape",
        "hash": "934ba5ff499035fa42a7815fb2e62daa7b39fe2f9362391236d1c27047dda935",
        "text": "nest(1) = {\"v\": 1}; nest(k) = {\"v\": nest(k - 1)}. So nest(3) = {\"v\": {\"v\": {\"v\": 1}}}: k dicts, with the integer 1 inside the innermost one.\nrequest = {\"model\": \"typesafe/jev-1.13\", \"state\": nest(k), \"questions\": {\"next\": {\"type\": \"choice\", \"instructions\": \"Pick.\", \"criteria\": {\"a\": \"A\", \"b\": \"B\"}}}}"
      },
      {
        "id": "doc",
        "hash": "090145105ebbbd1967c69f3088d78119941de0b8cd8c38e89ae8256caf92cf49",
        "text": "Jev state objects may nest up to 16 levels deep."
      },
